[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue and marked known. Its reports hold **three
problems**. The first fix will not close the other two.

<Callout>
Not one issue. Each problem has its own ticket in the results repo (issues 1, 2 and 3).
</Callout>

## What is in the ticket

<ProblemSplit ticket={4471} />

The export has overlapping pages, so some reports appear twice. Each report is counted once, by id.

## 1. Parser reads dates month first

Every tenant writes the day first, in every channel. The shared parser reads month first, so the
day and month come out flipped ("7 April" arrives as "4 July"). This is the problem #4471 describes,
and it is most of the ticket. It is not just the form: reports come by app, email and form.

## 2. The booking-v3 form hint

Three tenants run `booking-v3`, and its form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. Their people
type month first, as the hint says, and the form reads it the tenant's way. This is a different
bug with a different fix (the hint, not the parser), and it only shows up on the form channel.
Fixing the parser alone will not stop it.

## 3. One day off, not a flip

A few reports do not describe a swapped day and month. They describe a date that is one day off
(a Monday for a Tuesday, an invite sent before the booking, two clients in two cities getting
different days). This points to a time zone or midnight boundary problem. That is an inference: the
reports do not say. The desk note marks them as one-day moves, and tenant-based sorting files them
under the parser. They are a third problem. The fix for the first two will not touch them.

## Intake guessed wrong

Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser. That is a guess, and it is often not the
cause. The table below sorts by tenant (where they are and which form they run) and shows what
intake tagged.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What to change

- Keep the three tickets open and separate. Do not merge them back.
- Do not edit [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject). A decision is never edited
  after it is accepted. Propose a new record that replaces it: subject matching hid three bugs
  behind one count.
- Sort reports by tenant and channel before you merge, not by subject alone.

